# The release build COPYs argus/rootfs/ straight into the add-on image, and
# core.autocrlf=true on the release workstation rewrites the working tree to CRLF on
# checkout. A CRLF shebang is fatal in the container: `#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bashio`
# makes s6 exec a binary named "bashio", cont-init exits 127 and the add-on
# crash-loops with `exec: fatal: unable to exec bashio` + `: No such file or directory`.
# Pin the files that RUN inside the container to LF regardless of local git config.
# (detector/ is deliberately not listed: its .py files ship CRLF today and are started
# by an explicit `python3 -m`, never by shebang, so normalising them would be churn.)
argus/rootfs/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
